'''alcyonarian''' (al″si-ō-nā′ri-an), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< ''Alcyonaria'' + ''-an.''] '''I.''' ''a.'' Relating or pertaining to the order or to a member of the order ''Alcyonaria''. Equivalent terms are ''halcyonoid'' and ''asteroidal.''

'''II.''' ''n.'' One of the ''Alcyonaria'' (which see).
{{smaller block|Various forms of ''alcyonarians'', a special group of corals, were found at considerable depths.
{{right|''Science'', IV. 171.}}}}
Also written ''halcyonarian.''

